/-!
# Global generation and faithfully flat base change

Let `f : X ⟶ Spec A` be a quasi-compact quasi-separated morphism, let `Spec B ⟶ Spec A` be
flat and surjective, and let `F` be a quasi-coherent `𝒪_X`-module. Then `F` is generated by
its global sections if and only if its base change to `X ×_{Spec A} Spec B` is.

## Main results

* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.FlatBaseChange.pullbackGeneratingSections`: global generation is
  preserved by an arbitrary pullback; no flatness and no finiteness hypothesis is needed.
* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.FlatBaseChange.nonempty_generatingSections_pullback_iff`:
  **[Stacks, Tag 0B57], corrected.** For `X` quasi-compact and quasi-separated over `Spec A`,
  global generation of a quasi-coherent module is both preserved and reflected by a faithfully
  flat base change of the affine base. For a general `X` the statement is false:
  `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.FlatBaseChange.not_forall_nonempty_generatingSections_pullback_iff`.
* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.FlatBaseChange.nonempty_generatingSections_pullback_iff_specMap`:
  the same statement read on a faithfully flat ring map `A ⟶ B`.

## Implementation notes

Global generation is the nonemptiness of Mathlib's `SheafOfModules.GeneratingSections`, whose
index type is unrestricted; the reflecting direction produces the family of *all* global
sections, so nothing here assumes a finite generating family.

The reflecting direction runs on stalks. By
`AlgebraicGeometry.generates_iff_stalkwise_generates` a family of global sections generates a
module exactly when its germs span every stalk, so it suffices to span `F_x` for every `x` by
germs of global sections. Writing `p` for the base change of `Spec B ⟶ Spec A`, two inputs
combine. First, [Stacks, Tag 02KH] in degree zero over an affine base —
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.FlatBaseChange.exists_linearEquiv_sections_pushforward_pullback` —
exhibits `Γ(X', p^* F)` as `Γ(X, F) ⊗_A B`, so every global section of `p^* F` lies in the
`Γ(X', 𝒪_{X'})`-span of the pullbacks of global sections of `F`. Second, [Stacks, Tag 0098] —
`RingedSpaceModuleAdjunction.exists_modulePullbackStalkLinearEquiv` — identifies `(p^* F)_y`
with `𝒪_{X',y} ⊗_{𝒪_{X,p y}} F_{p y}`, carrying the germ of the pullback of a section to
`1 ⊗ₜ` its germ. Since `p` is flat and surjective the stalk map `𝒪_{X,p y} ⟶ 𝒪_{X',y}` is a
flat local homomorphism of local rings, hence faithfully flat, and a family whose pure tensors
span the base change already spans.

The structure sheaf has a `CommRingCat`-valued stalk and a `RingCat`-valued one. The stalkwise
criterion is stated over the latter and the base-change arguments need the former; the two are
bridged by `SemilinearStalk.commStalkRingEquiv` together with
`AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.commStalk_smul_eq`, and a spanning statement is transported
across by `Stacks.SheafOfModules.span_eq_top_of_ringEquiv`.

**The statement is false for a general morphism.** The Stacks Project states Tag 0B57 for an
arbitrary morphism `X ⟶ Spec A`; its proof computes `Γ(X_{A'}, F_{A'}) = Γ(X, F) ⊗_A A'` by
[Stacks, Tag 02KH], which needs `X ⟶ Spec A` quasi-compact and quasi-separated, and without
quasi-compactness the conclusion fails, as
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.FlatBaseChange.not_forall_nonempty_generatingSections_pullback_iff` and
its `_specMap` form show: over `A = ℤ`, with `A' = ℤ[1/3] × ℤ[1/2]`, one glues two copies of
`Spec ℤ` that are identified at the prime `3` by infinitely many charts, to every order, and takes
for `F` an invertible module that is trivial over `D(3)` and over `D(2)` but whose global sections
all vanish at a point over the prime `2`. The declarations below are therefore stated for
`X ⟶ Spec A` quasi-compact and quasi-separated, which covers every use of the tag in the Stacks
Project (proper schemes over a field). The preserving direction holds for an arbitrary pullback and
is stated separately.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0B57](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0B57)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 02KH](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/02KH)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01AN](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01AN)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0098](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0098)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory TopologicalSpace Limits Opposite AlgebraicGeometry
open Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.SectionsBaseChange
open scoped TensorProduct

universe u

namespace Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.FlatBaseChange

/-! ### Spanning families and faithfully flat base change -/

/-- **A family whose pure tensors span a faithfully flat base change already spans.** If
`R ⟶ S` is faithfully flat and the elements `1 ⊗ₜ s i` span `S ⊗[R] M` over `S`, then the
`s i` span `M` over `R`. -/
theorem span_eq_top_of_span_one_tmul_eq_top {R S M I : Type u} [CommRing R] [CommRing S]
    [AddCommGroup M] [Algebra R S] [Module R M] [Module.FaithfullyFlat R S] (s : I → M)
    (h : Submodule.span S (Set.range fun i ↦ (1 : S) ⊗ₜ[R] s i) = ⊤) :
    Submodule.span R (Set.range s) = ⊤ := by
  classical
  let φ : (I →₀ R) →ₗ[R] M := Finsupp.linearCombination R s
  have hrange : LinearMap.range (φ.baseChange S) = ⊤ := by
    refine top_unique ?_
    rw [← h]
    refine Submodule.span_le.mpr ?_
    rintro _ ⟨i, rfl⟩
    exact ⟨(1 : S) ⊗ₜ[R] Finsupp.single i 1, by simp [φ]⟩
  have hsurj : Function.Surjective (φ.lTensor S) := by
    rw [← LinearMap.baseChange_eq_lTensor]
    exact LinearMap.range_eq_top.mp hrange
  rw [← Finsupp.range_linearCombination]
  exact LinearMap.range_eq_top.mpr
    ((Module.FaithfullyFlat.lTensor_surjective_iff_surjective R S φ).mp hsurj)

/-- **The stalk map of a flat surjective morphism of schemes is faithfully flat**: it is a flat
local homomorphism of local rings. -/
theorem faithfullyFlat_stalkMap {X Y : Scheme.{u}} (p : X ⟶ Y) [Flat p] [Surjective p] (x : X) :
    (p.stalkMap x).hom.FaithfullyFlat := by
  algebraize [(p.stalkMap x).hom]
  exact @Module.FaithfullyFlat.of_flat_of_isLocalHom _ _ _ _ _ _ _
    (Flat.stalkMap p x) (p.toLRSHom.prop x)

/-! ### Global generation tested on stalks -/

section Stalkwise

variable {X : Scheme.{u}} (F : X.Modules)

/-- The germ at `x` of a global section of `F`. -/
abbrev germTop (x : X) (m : Γ(F, (⊤ : X.Opens))) :
    ToType (TopCat.Presheaf.stalk (C := AddCommGrpCat.{u}) F.val.presheaf x) :=
  (TopCat.Presheaf.Γgerm F.val.presheaf x).hom m

/-- The germ at `x` of the zero global section is zero. -/
@[simp]
lemma germTop_zero (x : X) : germTop F x 0 = 0 :=
  map_zero (TopCat.Presheaf.Γgerm F.val.presheaf x).hom

/-- The germ at `x` of a sum of global sections is the sum of their germs. -/
@[simp]
lemma germTop_add (x : X) (m n : Γ(F, (⊤ : X.Opens))) :
    germTop F x (m + n) = germTop F x m + germTop F x n :=
  map_add (TopCat.Presheaf.Γgerm F.val.presheaf x).hom m n

/-- Taking germs at `x` is semilinear along the germ map of the structure sheaf. -/
lemma germTop_smul (x : X) (r : Γ(X, (⊤ : X.Opens))) (m : Γ(F, (⊤ : X.Opens))) :
    germTop F x (r • m) = (X.presheaf.Γgerm x).hom r • germTop F x m :=
  PresheafOfModules.germ_smul (R := X.presheaf) F.val x ⊤ (Set.mem_univ x) r m

/-- **[Stacks, Tag 01AN] over the `CommRingCat`-valued stalk.** A family of global sections
generates a sheaf of modules on a scheme exactly when its germs span every stalk as a module
over the local ring there. -/
theorem generates_iff_span_germTop_eq_top {I : Type u} (s : I → F.sections) :
    Epi (F.freeHomEquiv.symm s) ↔
      ∀ x : X, Submodule.span (R := ToType (X.presheaf.stalk x))
        (Set.range fun i ↦ germTop F x ((s i).eval (op ⊤))) = ⊤ := by
  rw [generates_iff_stalkwise_generates X.ringCatSheaf F s]
  refine forall_congr' fun x ↦ ⟨fun h ↦ ?_, fun h ↦ ?_⟩
  · exact Stacks.SheafOfModules.span_eq_top_of_ringEquiv _ _
      (SemilinearStalk.commStalkRingEquiv X.presheaf x)
      (AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.commStalk_smul_eq X.presheaf x F.val) _ h
  · refine Stacks.SheafOfModules.span_eq_top_of_ringEquiv _ _
      (SemilinearStalk.commStalkRingEquiv X.presheaf x).symm (fun r m ↦ ?_) _ h
    exact (AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.commStalk_smul_eq X.presheaf x F.val
      ((SemilinearStalk.commStalkRingEquiv X.presheaf x).symm r) m).symm.trans
      (congrArg (fun z : ToType (X.presheaf.stalk x) ↦ z • m)
        ((SemilinearStalk.commStalkRingEquiv X.presheaf x).apply_symm_apply r))

/-- Every global section of a module on a scheme is the value at `⊤` of a restriction-compatible
family, because `⊤` is terminal in the site of opens. -/
theorem exists_sections_eval_top (m : Γ(F, (⊤ : X.Opens))) :
    ∃ s : F.sections, s.eval (op ⊤) = m :=
  ⟨(Stacks.SectionRingGeometric.sectionsEquivObj isTerminalTop F.val).symm m,
    (Stacks.SectionRingGeometric.sectionsEquivObj isTerminalTop F.val).apply_symm_apply m⟩

/-- The germs of the compatible families and the germs of the global sections of `F` at `x` are
the same set. -/
theorem range_germTop_eval (x : X) :
    (Set.range fun s : F.sections ↦ germTop F x (s.eval (op ⊤))) =
      Set.range fun m : Γ(F, (⊤ : X.Opens)) ↦ germTop F x m := by
  refine Set.Subset.antisymm ?_ ?_
  · rintro _ ⟨s, rfl⟩
    exact Set.mem_range_self _
  · rintro _ ⟨m, rfl⟩
    obtain ⟨s, hs⟩ := exists_sections_eval_top F m
    exact ⟨s, congrArg (germTop F x) hs⟩

/-- A sheaf of modules on a scheme whose stalks are spanned by the germs of its global sections
is generated by global sections. -/
theorem nonempty_generatingSections_of_span_germTop_eq_top
    (h : ∀ x : X, Submodule.span (R := ToType (X.presheaf.stalk x))
      (Set.range fun m : Γ(F, (⊤ : X.Opens)) ↦ germTop F x m) = ⊤) :
    Nonempty F.GeneratingSections :=
  ⟨⟨F.sections, id, (generates_iff_span_germTop_eq_top F id).2 fun x ↦
    (congrArg (Submodule.span _) (range_germTop_eval F x)).trans (h x)⟩⟩

/-- The germs of a generating family of global sections span every stalk. -/
theorem span_germTop_generatingSections_eq_top (G : F.GeneratingSections) (x : X) :
    Submodule.span (R := ToType (X.presheaf.stalk x))
      (Set.range fun i ↦ germTop F x ((G.s i).eval (op ⊤))) = ⊤ :=
  (generates_iff_span_germTop_eq_top F G.s).1 G.epi x

end Stalkwise

/-! ### Global generation is preserved by pullback -/

/-- **Global generation is preserved by pullback.** The pullback functor is a left adjoint
which takes the structure sheaf to the structure sheaf, so it carries a family of generating
global sections to one. -/
def pullbackGeneratingSections {X Y : Scheme.{u}} (p : X ⟶ Y) (F : Y.Modules)
    (G : F.GeneratingSections) : ((Scheme.Modules.pullback p).obj F).GeneratingSections := by
  change ((RingedSpaceModuleAdjunction.modulePullback p.toLRSHom.toShHom).obj F).GeneratingSections
  exact Stacks.SheafOfModules.modulePullbackGeneratingSections p.toLRSHom.toShHom F G

/-! ### Global generation is reflected by a faithfully flat base change -/

section Reflect

variable {A B : CommRingCat.{u}} {X X' : Scheme.{u}} {f : X ⟶ Spec A} {g : Spec B ⟶ Spec A}
  {f' : X' ⟶ Spec B} {g' : X' ⟶ X}

/-- The pullback of a global section of `F` along `g'`, as a global section of `(g')^* F`: the
unit of `(g')^* ⊣ (g')_*` read on global sections. -/
abbrev pullbackGlobalSection (g' : X' ⟶ X) (F : X.Modules) (a : Γ(F, (⊤ : X.Opens))) :
    Γ((Scheme.Modules.pullback g').obj F, (⊤ : X'.Opens)) :=
  pullbackUnitSections g' F ⊤ a

/-- **Every global section of the base change is a combination of pullbacks of global
sections.** This is [Stacks, Tag 02KH] in degree zero over an affine base: the global sections
of `(g')^* F` are `Γ(X, F) ⊗_A B`. -/
theorem mem_span_pullbackGlobalSection (H : IsPullback g' f' f g) [Flat g] [QuasiCompact f]
    [QuasiSeparated f] (F : X.Modules) [F.IsQuasicoherent]
    (t : Γ((Scheme.Modules.pullback g').obj F, (⊤ : X'.Opens))) :
    t ∈ Submodule.span Γ(X', (⊤ : X'.Opens)) (Set.range (pullbackGlobalSection g' F)) := by
  let _ : Algebra Γ(Spec A, (⊤ : (Spec A).Opens)) Γ(Spec B, (⊤ : (Spec B).Opens)) :=
    baseAlgebra g
  obtain ⟨e, he⟩ := exists_linearEquiv_sections_pushforward_pullback H F
  obtain ⟨z, rfl⟩ := e.surjective t
  induction z using TensorProduct.inductionOn with
  | add z w hz hw =>
      rw [map_add]
      exact Submodule.add_mem _ hz hw
  | tmul b a =>
      have hval : e (b ⊗ₜ[Γ(Spec A, (⊤ : (Spec A).Opens))] a) =
          f'.appTop.hom b • pullbackGlobalSection g' F a := by
        rw [he b a]
        exact congrArg (fun z ↦ f'.appTop.hom b • z) (pullbackSectionsHom_top g' F a)
      rw [hval]
      exact Submodule.smul_mem _ _ (Submodule.subset_span ⟨a, rfl⟩)

/-- A semilinear additive map sends the span of a set into a submodule that contains the image
of the set. -/
private lemma map_mem_of_mem_span_of_smul {R S M N : Type*} [Semiring R] [Semiring S]
    [AddCommMonoid M] [AddCommMonoid N] [Module R M] [Module S N] (σ : R →+* S) (f : M →+ N)
    (hf : ∀ (r : R) (m : M), f (r • m) = σ r • f m) {s : Set M} {T : Submodule S N}
    (h : ∀ m ∈ s, f m ∈ T) {m : M} (hm : m ∈ Submodule.span R s) : f m ∈ T := by
  induction hm using Submodule.span_induction with
  | mem m hm => exact h m hm
  | zero => simp
  | add z w _ _ hz hw => simpa using T.add_mem hz hw
  | smul r z _ hz => rw [hf]; exact T.smul_mem _ hz

/-- The germs of the pullbacks of the global sections of `F` span every stalk of `(g')^* F`,
as soon as `(g')^* F` is generated by global sections. -/
theorem span_germTop_pullbackGlobalSection_eq_top (H : IsPullback g' f' f g) [Flat g]
    [QuasiCompact f] [QuasiSeparated f] (F : X.Modules) [F.IsQuasicoherent]
    (G : ((Scheme.Modules.pullback g').obj F).GeneratingSections) (y : X') :
    Submodule.span (R := ToType (X'.presheaf.stalk y))
      (Set.range fun a : Γ(F, (⊤ : X.Opens)) ↦
        germTop ((Scheme.Modules.pullback g').obj F) y (pullbackGlobalSection g' F a)) = ⊤ := by
  set P := (Scheme.Modules.pullback g').obj F
  refine top_unique ?_
  rw [← span_germTop_generatingSections_eq_top P G y]
  refine Submodule.span_le.mpr ?_
  rintro _ ⟨i, rfl⟩
  exact map_mem_of_mem_span_of_smul (X'.presheaf.Γgerm y).hom _ (germTop_smul P y)
    (by rintro _ ⟨a, rfl⟩; exact Submodule.subset_span (Set.mem_range_self a))
    (mem_span_pullbackGlobalSection H F _)

/-- The germs of the global sections of `F` span the stalk of `F` at any point in the image of
`g'`, as soon as `(g')^* F` is generated by global sections. -/
theorem span_germTop_eq_top_of_generatingSections_pullback (H : IsPullback g' f' f g) [Flat g]
    [Surjective g] [QuasiCompact f] [QuasiSeparated f] (F : X.Modules) [F.IsQuasicoherent]
    (G : ((Scheme.Modules.pullback g').obj F).GeneratingSections) (x : X) :
    Submodule.span (R := ToType (X.presheaf.stalk x))
      (Set.range fun a : Γ(F, (⊤ : X.Opens)) ↦ germTop F x a) = ⊤ := by
  have : Flat g' := MorphismProperty.of_isPullback H.flip inferInstance
  have : Surjective g' := MorphismProperty.of_isPullback H.flip inferInstance
  obtain ⟨y, rfl⟩ := g'.surjective x
  let : Algebra (ToType (X.presheaf.stalk (g' y))) (ToType (X'.presheaf.stalk y)) :=
    (g'.stalkMap y).hom.toAlgebra
  have : Module.FaithfullyFlat (ToType (X.presheaf.stalk (g' y)))
      (ToType (X'.presheaf.stalk y)) := faithfullyFlat_stalkMap g' y
  obtain ⟨e, he⟩ :=
    RingedSpaceModuleAdjunction.exists_modulePullbackStalkLinearEquiv g'.toLRSHom.toShHom F y
  let e' : ToType (TopCat.Presheaf.stalk (C := AddCommGrpCat.{u})
        ((Scheme.Modules.pullback g').obj F).val.presheaf y) ≃ₗ[ToType (X'.presheaf.stalk y)]
      ToType (X'.presheaf.stalk y) ⊗[ToType (X.presheaf.stalk (g' y))]
        ToType (TopCat.Presheaf.stalk (C := AddCommGrpCat.{u}) F.val.presheaf (g' y)) := e
  refine span_eq_top_of_span_one_tmul_eq_top (S := ToType (X'.presheaf.stalk y)) _ ?_
  refine top_unique fun z _ ↦ ?_
  obtain ⟨w, rfl⟩ := e'.surjective z
  exact map_mem_of_mem_span_of_smul (RingHom.id _) e'.toAddMonoidHom e'.map_smul
    (by
      rintro _ ⟨a, rfl⟩
      exact (he ⊤ (Set.mem_univ _) a).symm ▸ Submodule.subset_span (Set.mem_range_self a))
    ((span_germTop_pullbackGlobalSection_eq_top H F G y).ge Submodule.mem_top)

/-- **[Stacks, Tag 0B57], corrected.** Let `f : X ⟶ Spec A` be a quasi-compact quasi-separated
morphism, let `g : Spec B ⟶ Spec A` be flat and surjective — equivalently, a faithfully flat
ring map `A ⟶ B` — and let `F` be a quasi-coherent `𝒪_X`-module. Then `F` is generated by
global sections if and only if its base change along `g` is.

The correction is the quasi-compactness and quasi-separatedness of `f`, which the Stacks Project
does not assume. Without quasi-compactness the equivalence fails:
`not_forall_nonempty_generatingSections_pullback_iff` gives a quasi-coherent module on a scheme
over `Spec ℤ` which is not generated by global sections, while its base change along the
faithfully flat `ℤ ⟶ ℤ[1/3] × ℤ[1/2]` is. That scheme is quasi-separated, so it does not show
that quasi-separatedness of `f` is needed; it is the hypothesis of [Stacks, Tag 02KH]. -/
@[stacks 0B57 "corrected: for `X ⟶ Spec A` quasi-compact and quasi-separated; without \
quasi-compactness the statement is false, see \
`not_forall_nonempty_generatingSections_pullback_iff`"]
theorem nonempty_generatingSections_pullback_iff (H : IsPullback g' f' f g) [Flat g]
    [Surjective g] [QuasiCompact f] [QuasiSeparated f] (F : X.Modules) [F.IsQuasicoherent] :
    Nonempty F.GeneratingSections ↔
      Nonempty ((Scheme.Modules.pullback g').obj F).GeneratingSections :=
  ⟨fun ⟨G⟩ ↦ ⟨pullbackGeneratingSections g' F G⟩, fun ⟨G⟩ ↦
    nonempty_generatingSections_of_span_germTop_eq_top F
      (span_germTop_eq_top_of_generatingSections_pullback H F G)⟩

end Reflect

/-- **[Stacks, Tag 0B57], corrected, read on a faithfully flat ring map.** For a faithfully
flat ring map `φ : A ⟶ B` and a quasi-coherent module `F` on a scheme quasi-compact and
quasi-separated over `Spec A`, global generation of `F` is equivalent to global generation of
the base change of `F` to `X ×_{Spec A} Spec B`.

The correction is the quasi-compactness and quasi-separatedness of `X ⟶ Spec A`, which the
Stacks Project does not assume. Without quasi-compactness the equivalence fails:
`not_forall_nonempty_generatingSections_pullback_iff_specMap` is the negation of this statement
with those two hypotheses removed. -/
@[stacks 0B57 "corrected, on a faithfully flat ring map: for `X ⟶ Spec A` quasi-compact and \
quasi-separated; without quasi-compactness the statement is false, see \
`not_forall_nonempty_generatingSections_pullback_iff_specMap`"]
theorem nonempty_generatingSections_pullback_iff_specMap {A B : CommRingCat.{u}} (φ : A ⟶ B)
    (hφ : φ.hom.FaithfullyFlat) {X : Scheme.{u}} (f : X ⟶ Spec A) [QuasiCompact f]
    [QuasiSeparated f] (F : X.Modules) [F.IsQuasicoherent] :
    Nonempty F.GeneratingSections ↔
      Nonempty (((Scheme.Modules.pullback
        (Limits.pullback.fst f (Spec.map φ))).obj F).GeneratingSections) :=
  have : Flat (Spec.map φ) := ((flat_and_surjective_SpecMap_iff φ).2 hφ).1
  have : Surjective (Spec.map φ) := ((flat_and_surjective_SpecMap_iff φ).2 hφ).2
  nonempty_generatingSections_pullback_iff (IsPullback.of_hasPullback f (Spec.map φ)) F

end Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.FlatBaseChange

end
